   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 9 · Part separation → PSD\nSee-through (SIGGRAPH 2026) decomposes the source canvas into up to 24 semantic layers **with the hidden parts painted in** (face under the bangs, back hair, eye whites…) and orders them by depth.\n\n`StandRig Layers To PSD` maps them back to the source canvas, renames tags (hairf → Front Hair, eyewhite-l → Eye White L; L/R = character's own side), adds the expression variants as hidden layers and writes `output/standrig/<project>/<name>.psd` with ag-psd-compatible folders.\n\nNeeds the custom node pack **ComfyUI-See-through** (models auto-download from Hugging Face, ~16 GB VRAM at 1280; use nf4 / group_offload for 8–12 GB).\n\n**Low-memory settings** (8 GB VRAM / 16 GB RAM): 4-bit nf4 models (smaller download, ~8 GB VRAM), group offload, 1024 px layers, 720 px depth. Slower, but it fits. The first run downloads the nf4 models from Hugging Face; that shows as 0 % in the queue, watch the console."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
